  "findings": [
    "SequenceDiagram.activate assigns a single pendingCreate field; addMessage attaches and clears only that one event. Rust sequence_create_message_indices stores a Vec of pending IDs, so two consecutive creates are incorrectly queued and consumed by separate future messages. The account invariant that every pending CREATE survives is too strong.",
    "Java-valid double-pending same-participant input has two Roe label occurrences (one created head plus tail); Rust before also has two, but candidate has three. This is an introduced semantic regression inside a case already failing whole SVG before: zero lost whole-case passes does not mean zero regressions. Different-participant pending overwrite fails in both engines too.",
    "Repeated creates separated by compatible messages, three iterations, multiline actors, reverse queues and active group scope support the intended event-vs-lifeline separation. LifeLine.setCreate and LivingSpace.goCreate overwrite the final origin; CommunicationTile.drawU translates the complete head. Five of ten fresh whole cases pass; reverse created queue legacy still has width213 versus Java223."
  ],
